[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Longest Suspension Bridge in the World]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.29]Lesson 17 | 第17课
[00:02.83]The longest suspension bridge in the world | 世界上最长的吊桥
[00:12.30]How is the bridge supported? | 这座桥靠什么支撑？
[00:16.67]Verrazano, an Italian about whom little is known, sailed into New York Harbour in 1524 and named it Angouleme. | 1524年，一位鲜为人知的意大利人维拉萨诺驾船驶进纽约港，将该港命名为安古拉姆。
[00:28.43]He described it as 'a very agreeable situation located within two small hills in the midst of which flowed a great river.' | 他对该港作了这样的描述：“地理位置十分宜人，位于两座小山之间，一条大河从中间流过。”
[00:39.43]Though Verrazano is by no means considered to be a great explorer, his name will probably remain immortal, | 虽然维拉萨诺绝对算不上一个伟大的探险家，但他的名字将会流芳百世，
[00:48.07]for on November 21st, 1964, the longest suspension bridge in the world was named after him. | 因为1964年11月21日建成的一座世界上最长的吊桥是以他的名字命名的。
[00:59.32]The Verrazano Bridge, which was designed by Othmar Ammann, joins Brooklyn to Staten Island. | 维拉萨诺大桥由奥斯马·阿曼设计，连接布鲁克林与斯塔滕岛。
[01:07.72]It has a span of 4, 260 feet. | 桥长4260英尺。
[01:12.52]The bridge is so long that the shape of the earth had to be taken into account by its designer. | 桥身如此之长，设计师不得不考虑地球的形状。
[01:19.92]Two great towers support four huge cables. | 两座巨塔支撑着四根粗大的缆索。
[01:25.53]The towers are built on immense underwater platforms made of steel and concrete. | 塔身建在巨大的水下钢盘混凝土平台上。
[01:32.28]The platforms extend to a depth of over 100 feet under the sea. | 平台深入水下100多英尺。
[01:37.65]These alone took sixteen months to build. | 仅建造这两座塔就用了16个月时间。
[01:41.48]Above the surface of the water, the towers rise to a height of nearly 700 feet. | 塔身高出水面将近700英尺。
[01:48.25]They support the cables from which the bridge has been suspended. | 高塔支撑着吊桥悬吊所用的缆索。
[01:52.62]Each of the four cables contains 26, 108 lengths of wire. | 四根缆索中的每一根都包含26108根钢丝。
[01:59.62]It has been estimated that if the bridge were packed with cars, it would still only be carrying a third of its total capacity. | 据估计，即使桥上挤满了汽车，也只承载了总承载能力的三分之一。
[02:09.73]However, size and strength are not the only important things about this bridge. | 然而，这座桥的重要特点不仅是它的规模和强度。
[02:15.93]Despite its immensity, it is both simple and elegant, | 尽管此桥很大，但它结构简单，造型雅致，
[02:21.49]fulfilling its designer's dream to creat 'an enormous object drawn as faintly as possible'. | 实现了设计师创造“一个用尽可能细的线条勾勒出的庞然大物”的梦想。
